<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Shomer Sachar<br>[Laws of a Paid Guardian]</div>
<div class="sub-sub">And in it will be explained the matter of Chanukah</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Halacha 2 &mdash; Part A (&sect;&sect;1&ndash;4)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;1</div>

<p>Based on the Torah teaching: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the ravens I have commanded to sustain you&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Melachim I 17:4)</span> &mdash; in Likutay Tinyana, siman 4. See there the entire matter.</p>

<p>And the rule, in brief: through tzedakah one merits to subdue the <span class="key-term">maitzach hanachash</span> [the forehead of the serpent], which is the root of the wisdom of nature [chochmas hateva]. Which draws sustenance from the elders of the generation who lack completeness. For the essential old age is to increase each and every day holy light and da&rsquo;as &mdash; so that each day that comes afterward should shine more in the service of Hashem. But when one does not increase holy light and da&rsquo;as each day, then even when he ages he is called &ldquo;short of days&rdquo; [k&rsquo;tzar yamim]. And from such elders who lack completeness, the forehead of the serpent draws sustenance &mdash; the root of the wisdom of nature.</p>

<p>And through tzedakah, the sustenance of the forehead of the serpent, the root of the wisdom of nature, is nullified. And then the <span class="key-term">maitzach haratzon</span> [the forehead of the Will] is revealed &mdash; which draws sustenance from the holy elders, the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;elder and of uplifted countenance,&rdquo;</span> as is explained there.</p>

<p>And then the voice of the calling of the Yamim Tovim [holy festivals], the <span class="key-term">mikra&rsquo;ai kodesh</span>, is revealed and heard &mdash; which call and reveal the Ratzon [Divine Will]. See there.</p>

<p>And through the revelation of the Ratzon &mdash; that it is revealed that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, and there is no compulsion of nature at all &mdash; through this, yir&rsquo;ah [awe/fear] is made. And the yir&rsquo;ah is a vessel to receive the bestowal of chesed [kindness] that flows constantly.</p>

<p>And then, when His kindness flows upon us, one does not need to do any business or labor or trade for the sake of sustenance, for it is fulfilled: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And strangers shall stand and tend your flocks, and foreigners shall be your plowmen and your vinedressers; and you shall be called the priests of Hashem,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 61:5&ndash;6)</span> &mdash; see there.</p>

<p>It emerges that through tzedakah one merits that one does not need to spend time on any business or labor or trade for the sake of sustenance, and one can engage in the service of Hashem always. And through tzedakah one merits to widen all the openings [p&rsquo;sachim] of all the beginnings. For all beginnings are difficult, for at the time of the beginning one needs to make an opening anew &mdash; see there. And through tzedakah, all the openings that one needs to make at the time of the beginning are widened, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;You shall surely open&rdquo;</span> [pasoach tiftach] <span class="inline-source">(Devarim 15:8)</span> &mdash; see there, all of this is explained well.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;2</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of Chanukah. For the essential Chanukah is to subdue the wicked kingdom of Yavan [Greece], which rose against Israel to make them forget Your Torah, etc. For the wicked kingdom of Yavan is the aspect of the sages of nature, whose entire wisdom is called the wisdom of Yavan [Greek wisdom]. And they wanted to overpower Israel and to nullify the Torah, G&ndash;d forbid, and to make the wisdom of nature dominant in the world, G&ndash;d forbid.</p>

<p>For the entire Torah is the aspect of emunas haratzon [the faith of the Will] &mdash; that we believe that everything is according to His will, blessed be He &mdash; which is the foundation of the entire Torah, as is known. And they wanted to nullify emunas haratzon, G&ndash;d forbid, the totality of the Torah, and to draw, G&ndash;d forbid, the wisdom of nature.</p>

<p>And therefore we must in each and every generation, in each and every year, subdue the wicked kingdom of Yavan &mdash; that is, the wisdom of nature &mdash; during these holy days of Chanukah. And the essential subjugation of the wisdom of nature and the intensification of the revelation of the Ratzon is through connecting all the desires [r&rsquo;tzonos] to the root of the Ratzon, which is the aspect of the maitzach haratzon [the forehead of the Will], which intensifies through the holy elders of the generation, as above.</p>

<p>And the essential old age of holiness is the aspect of <span class="key-term">zakain</span> &mdash; &ldquo;this one has acquired wisdom&rdquo; [zeh kanah chochmah]. That is, to increase each day holy light and da&rsquo;as. For so must a person conduct himself all the days of his life &mdash; that each and every day that he ages further, he should shine more in the service of Hashem. And on each and every day of the days of his life that comes afterward, he should increase in it more holy light and da&rsquo;as. And this is the essential old age of holiness, through which the Ratzon intensifies, in the aspect of &ldquo;elder and of uplifted countenance.&rdquo;</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the kindling of the Chanukah light. For the oil of the Chanukah light &mdash; this is the aspect of the light of the da&rsquo;as, the aspect of the holy anointing oil [shemen mishchas kodesh], through which one draws the light of da&rsquo;as on each and every day. And each and every day one adds and goes, for the Chanukah light adds and goes [mosaif v&rsquo;holaich]. For each and every day that comes afterward must shine more, as above &mdash; and this is the essential old age of holiness, as above. And this is the aspect of the oil of the Chanukah light, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Like the good oil upon the head, that descends upon the beard, the beard of Aharon,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 133:2)</span>.</p>

<p>And through this the Ratzon is revealed and the wisdom of nature, the aspect of the wisdom of Yavan, is subdued &mdash; and this is the essential aspect of Chanukah, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;3</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the eight days of Chanukah. For it is necessary that all the seven days &mdash; which are the aspect of the seven days of building, the seven days of Creation &mdash; all should be illuminated from the eighth day, which is the aspect of the World to Come, which is above time, which is the aspect of &ldquo;a day that is entirely long and good.&rdquo; For there is the essential old age of holiness.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The days of our years, among them are seventy years; and if with might, eighty years&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 90:10)</span> &mdash; which are the essential old age. For seventy years are the aspect of the seven days of building. And the essential old age is above seventy years, which is the aspect of above time. For above the seven days of building, which are the aspect of time, the aspect of seventy years &mdash; above them is the aspect of Binah, <span class="key-term">Ima Ila&rsquo;ah</span> [the Supernal Mother], which is the aspect of the eighth day. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and if with might, eighty years.&rdquo; And from there is the essential old age. For there is the aspect of length of days and years &mdash; for it is the aspect of the World to Come, &ldquo;a day that is entirely long.&rdquo;</p>

<p>And therefore Moshe Rabbainu, who is the essential revelation of the Ratzon &mdash; for he revealed that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, through all the signs and wonders that he did before the eyes of Pharaoh, etc., in the Exodus from Egypt and the splitting of the Sea of Reeds and the giving of the Torah &mdash; therefore Moshe was eighty years old when he stood before Pharaoh. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;and if with might, eighty years&rdquo; &mdash; which is the essential old age, through which is the revelation of the Ratzon, as above. And therefore Moshe departed on Shabbos at Minchah, at the time of the Ratzon of the Ratzonos [ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin], as is known and as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For the essential revelation of the Ratzon is through him &mdash; for he is the aspect of the holy elder, etc.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the eight days of Chanukah, during which we draw the light of the holy elders through the oil of Chanukah, the aspect of: &ldquo;Like the good oil upon the head, that descends upon the beard,&rdquo; etc., as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;4</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the tzedakah of Chanukah &mdash; that all of Israel have the custom to give much tzedakah during Chanukah. For through tzedakah one subdues the forehead of the serpent, which draws sustenance from the elders of the generation who lack completeness, as above &mdash; so that the forehead of the serpent should not overpower against the forehead of the Will, G&ndash;d forbid. And this is accomplished only through tzedakah, as is explained well in the Torah teaching mentioned above.</p>

<p>It emerges that the essential subjugation of the forehead of the serpent, the root of the wisdom of nature, is through tzedakah. Therefore one gives much tzedakah during Chanukah &mdash; in order to subdue the forehead of the serpent that draws sustenance from the elders of the generation who lack completeness, and to make dominant the root of the Ratzon, which intensifies through the holy elders, who add light and da&rsquo;as each and every day as they grow older. And this is the aspect of the Chanukah light, the aspect of: the Chanukah light adds and goes, etc.</p>

<p>And through tzedakah, the openings of all the beginnings are widened, and one can begin in the service of Hashem. And therefore it is called &ldquo;Chanukah&rdquo; &mdash; which is an expression of <span class="key-term">chinuch</span> [inauguration/education], in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Educate [chanoch] the youth according to his way&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Mishlai 22:6)</span>. For then one can be initiated, to begin in the service of Hashem. For tzedakah is the beginning of all beginnings, as is explained there &mdash; see there.</p>

